c) produce counts in fixed order (lines, words, bytes).\n   114→    inputs:\n   115→      args: [\"-w\", \"-l\", \"-c\"]\n   116→      stdin: \"one two\\nthree\\n\"\n   117→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   118→    normalization: none\n   119→    expected:\n   120→      exit_code: 0\n   121→      stdout_structure: counts in order lines, words, bytes regardless of flag order\n   122→      stderr: \"\"\n   123→    traces:\n   124→      - prd005-wc R2.6\n   125→\n   126→  - name: wc_multi_file_total\n   127→    description: 'Two files produce per-file lines and a total line with right-aligned columns. Setup: file1.txt contains \"hello\\nworld\\n\" (2 lines, 2 words, 12 bytes), file2.txt contains \"foo bar baz\\n\" (1 line, 3 words, 12 bytes)'\n   128→    inputs:\n   129→      args: [\"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"]\n   130→      stdin: null\n   131→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   132→    normalization: none\n   133→    expected:\n   134→      exit_code: 0\n   135→      stdout_structure: three lines — file1 counts, file2 counts, total with label \"total\"; columns right-aligned\n   136→      stderr: \"\"\n   137→    traces:\n   138→      - prd005-wc R1.4\n   139→      - prd005-wc R3.1\n   140→      - prd005-wc R3.2\n   141→\n   142→  - name: wc_total_only\n   143→    description: '--total=only with two files prints only the total line. Setup: file1.txt contains \"a\\n\", file2.txt contains \"b\\nc\\n\"'\n   144→    inputs:\n   145→      args: [\"--total=only\", \"file1.txt\", \"file2.txt\"]\n   146→      stdin: null\n   147→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   148→    normalization: none\n   149→    expected:\n   150→      exit_code: 0\n   151→      stdout_structure: one line with summed counts and label \"total\"\n   152→      stderr: \"\"\n   153→    traces:\n   154→      - prd005-wc R3.3\n   155→\n   156→  - name: wc_total_never\n   157→    description: '--total=never with two files prints no total line. Setup: file1.txt contains \"x\\n\", file2.txt contains \"y\\n\"'\n   158→    in